    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0458" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg334"/>

                <head>No. 191.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chen Lan
                            Pin to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 25, 1881</date>.
                        (Received February 25.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor on the 21st ultimo to send
                    your excellency a communication upon the subject of the riot at Denver, Colo.,
                    which resulted in the loss of life and the destruction of property owned by the
                    Chinese residents.</p>
                <pb facs="0459" n="335" xml:id="pg335"/>
                <p>I shall be greatly obliged, Mr. Secretary, if I may soon receive a reply thereto,
                    that I may communicate the same to my government.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the renewed assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>CHEN LAN PIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
